# FlipFlapp Android

Native Kotlin/Compose client for the FlipFlapp football-event MVP. Read [docs/PROJECT.md](../../docs/PROJECT.md) for scope.

## Workflow

1. [docs/DOMAIN.md](../../docs/DOMAIN.md) — mobile domain interpretation
2. [docs/API.md](../../docs/API.md) — Rails `/api/v1` contract
3. [docs/TESTING.md](../../docs/TESTING.md) — clarify → tests → code
4. [docs/KOTLIN_STYLEGUIDE.md](../../docs/KOTLIN_STYLEGUIDE.md) — Kotlin/Compose conventions
5. [docs/DESIGN.md](../../docs/DESIGN.md) — Material 3 dark olive+gold / accessibility

## Hard limits

- Native only: Jetpack Compose, no WebView hybrid shell
- Rails owns domain rules and authorization; client checks are UX only
- JWT in EncryptedSharedPreferences / Keystore — never plain preferences
- No dependency, SDK, commit, or push unless explicitly requested
- Technical text in English; UI copy via string resources (French first)

